  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Oracle Health Government Services has $1.3B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Oracle Health Government Services won 28 awards in that period, with an average award size of $47.2M. Obligations are up 31.4% year over year. Obligations by fiscal year show $971M in FY21, $2B in FY22, $825M in FY23, $893M in FY24, $1B in FY25, and $1.3B in FY26. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the top buying agency with $1.3B in obligations. Computer Systems Design Services is the top market with $1.3B in obligations, followed by Computer Facilities Management Services with $3.6M and Used Household and Office Goods Moving with $110K. FY2026 totals are partial and reported fiscal year to date.",
